        "original_id": "1f54e314-e936-5217-b9c8-79760ee7d37a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 2011 Military Bowl, 2011–12 NCAA bowl season\n- Places: Robert F. Kennedy Memorial Stadium, Washington, D.C.\n- Teams: 2011 Toledo Rockets football team, 2011 Air Force Falcons football team, U.S. men's national soccer team\n- Topics: college football bowl games, stadium match history\n\nFacts:\n- The 2011 Military Bowl Presented by Northrop Grumman was the fourth edition of the game and was a postseason American college football bowl game in the 2011–12 NCAA bowl season.\n- The 2011 Military Bowl was held on December 28, 2011, at Robert F. Kennedy Memorial Stadium in Washington, D.C.\n- The 2011 Toledo Rockets football team was invited to the Military Bowl and defeated Air Force 42–41.\n- The 2011 Air Force Falcons football team was invited to the Military Bowl and lost to Toledo by a score of 42–41.\n- Robert F. Kennedy Memorial Stadium hosted 22 matches played by the U.S. men's national soccer team from 1977 to 2013, more than any other stadium.",
